# This scenario SIGKILLs the serving worker on kill-lifecycle steps, so the
# master legitimately logs
#   [alert] <master>#0: worker process <pid> exited on signal 9
# which prober_scrape_log (run by run-scenario.sh AFTER the driver, in the
# parent process) would otherwise treat as a server-side failure and red the
# whole scenario at full-green TAP. Exempt exactly that line -- and ONLY that
# line. Must live in `env` (sourced pre-boot by run-scenario.sh), NOT be
# exported from driver.sh: the driver runs in a subprocess and its exports never
# reach the parent's scrape (worker-death's env-file lesson).
#
# The regex is pinned to "exited on signal 9": a FAULT signal (SIGSEGV=11,
# SIGABRT=6, SIGBUS=7) carries an [alert] this pattern does NOT match, so it
# stays un-exempted and reds the log scrape -- the backstop to the driver's C2
# checkpoint (no forbidden death). Blanket-allowing all alerts would throw that
# backstop away. An extra signal-9 line is exempted here too ("[0-9]+" matches
# any pid); the protection against an unexpected additional kill is C2's exact
# EXPECT_SIG9 count comparison, not this exemption.
PROBER_ALLOW_LOG='worker process [0-9]+ exited on signal 9'
